WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.028 --> 00:00:02.550
- It's super frustrating when people don't

00:00:02.730 --> 00:00:05.030
have any idea as to what
they're applying for.

00:00:05.165 --> 00:00:07.748
(upbeat music)

00:00:09.910 --> 00:00:10.843
I'm a recruiter.

00:00:10.850 --> 00:00:14.490
- I've been recruiting in New
York City for about six years.

00:00:14.490 --> 00:00:16.940
- And this is what you
need to know to get hired.

00:00:18.660 --> 00:00:20.890
- When we get a resume,
we get super excited.

00:00:20.890 --> 00:00:22.620
I've got a great position open.

00:00:22.620 --> 00:00:25.620
My VP comes to me and he goes
oh my God, this is the guy.

00:00:25.620 --> 00:00:28.441
We have contacts at said companies

00:00:28.441 --> 00:00:30.084
that this person has worked at.

00:00:30.084 --> 00:00:34.060
Come to find out, this
person never worked there.

00:00:34.060 --> 00:00:36.890
- Someone told us that they graduated

00:00:36.890 --> 00:00:39.273
with a Bachelor's Degree.

00:00:39.273 --> 00:00:41.409
We ended up doing a background check.

00:00:41.409 --> 00:00:45.260
It came back that they
didn't go to college at all,

00:00:45.260 --> 00:00:46.990
and we had to rescind the offer.

00:00:46.990 --> 00:00:48.040
- Don't lie (laughs).

00:00:50.270 --> 00:00:53.070
- First off, a resume
should always be one page.

00:00:53.070 --> 00:00:55.140
- I always recommend that your resume

00:00:55.140 --> 00:00:56.896
should not be longer than two pages.

00:00:56.896 --> 00:00:59.190
- The most important
information on the top, right?

00:00:59.190 --> 00:01:00.760
Things that you're most proud about,

00:01:00.760 --> 00:01:02.340
and then what's your work experience.

00:01:02.340 --> 00:01:06.430
- When I see fonts like
Comic Sans, Wingdings,

00:01:07.590 --> 00:01:11.803
any sort of weird formatting
symbolism in your resume,

00:01:11.860 --> 00:01:14.620
I am probably not going
to move you forward.

00:01:14.620 --> 00:01:16.570
- The worst ones are ones that either

00:01:16.570 --> 00:01:19.840
are way too complicated and
have too much information

00:01:19.840 --> 00:01:21.770
that has nothing to do
with what I'm looking for

00:01:21.770 --> 00:01:23.700
or they're too simplified.

00:01:23.700 --> 00:01:25.860
- I literally got a resume once that said

00:01:26.140 --> 00:01:29.150
I don't need a resume, my
background will speak for itself,

00:01:29.150 --> 00:01:31.563
call me, and they did not get the job.

00:01:33.260 --> 00:01:36.260
- The worst phone calls are
when you get on the phone,

00:01:36.260 --> 00:01:37.100
why'd you apply?

00:01:37.100 --> 00:01:38.690
What do you know about my company?

00:01:38.690 --> 00:01:39.990
And you have nothing.

00:01:39.990 --> 00:01:42.560
- Absolutely do your
research, it's so important.

00:01:42.560 --> 00:01:44.913
Get on GlassDoor, get on their website.

00:01:47.040 --> 00:01:49.890
- If you're sick, do not
come in to a job interview.

00:01:49.890 --> 00:01:52.710
There was this one time I
was confirming an interview

00:01:52.800 --> 00:01:55.520
and they told me, they were
like okay, I have pink eye.

00:01:55.520 --> 00:01:57.143
I'm gonna wear an eye patch.

00:01:57.180 --> 00:01:58.363
I hope that's okay.

00:01:58.380 --> 00:01:59.653
Totally okay.

00:01:59.690 --> 00:02:02.960
She ended up coming in, and
she didn't wear an eye patch.

00:02:02.960 --> 00:02:04.933
Just call out, just stay home.

00:02:05.420 --> 00:02:06.820
Don't come in with pink eye.

00:02:08.980 --> 00:02:10.820
- I work in an office that is...

00:02:10.820 --> 00:02:12.830
I'll call it business comfortable.

00:02:12.830 --> 00:02:13.910
I want you to represent that.

00:02:13.910 --> 00:02:16.150
I want you to feel like
you could slide in,

00:02:16.150 --> 00:02:17.920
and that's what we're
looking for, visually.

00:02:17.920 --> 00:02:21.737
- I would probably research
and go onto the LinkedIn page

00:02:21.737 --> 00:02:25.576
and the company's page
to see how they dress.

00:02:25.576 --> 00:02:27.100
- If we're super casual

00:02:27.100 --> 00:02:29.350
and you're coming in
with a three piece suit,

00:02:29.980 --> 00:02:31.190
probably not gonna work out.

00:02:31.190 --> 00:02:32.365
- It is too damn much.

00:02:32.365 --> 00:02:36.123
Don't do that, don't do that.

00:02:37.590 --> 00:02:39.994
- When we ask about
your greatest weakness,

00:02:39.994 --> 00:02:42.041
usually I'm just asking to see

00:02:42.041 --> 00:02:44.070
how honest you are with yourself.

00:02:44.070 --> 00:02:47.110
Things that will help me
understand that you are generally

00:02:47.210 --> 00:02:50.350
paying attention to who
your inner person is.

00:02:50.350 --> 00:02:51.430
That's important to hear.

00:02:51.430 --> 00:02:55.630
- A good answer for your
weakness should be genuine.

00:02:55.630 --> 00:02:57.950
What is an actual weakness
that you wanna work on,

00:02:57.950 --> 00:02:59.710
and tell us how and why.

00:02:59.710 --> 00:03:00.700
- So, for example,

00:03:00.700 --> 00:03:03.540
if your greatness weakness is
that you can't get up on time,

00:03:03.540 --> 00:03:06.070
you should finish your answer
by saying that's my weakness,

00:03:06.070 --> 00:03:08.120
but this is what I'm doing to work on it.

00:03:10.500 --> 00:03:12.580
- The first conversation
I have with candidates

00:03:12.580 --> 00:03:13.680
is always about money.

00:03:13.740 --> 00:03:14.750
- There is a line, right?

00:03:14.750 --> 00:03:16.600
There's a cap, and then there's a floor.

00:03:16.600 --> 00:03:19.481
- If you want 20 grand
more than the job offers,

00:03:19.481 --> 00:03:21.150
then that's a conversation you should have

00:03:21.150 --> 00:03:23.400
from the very beginning so
there's full transparency

00:03:23.400 --> 00:03:24.810
between all parties.

00:03:24.810 --> 00:03:26.270
- You're not getting underpaid, right?

00:03:26.270 --> 00:03:28.173
So, imagine a tree.

00:03:28.440 --> 00:03:30.190
You might fit in the middle, right?

00:03:30.260 --> 00:03:33.867
And if that middle, let's
just call it $50,000,

00:03:33.940 --> 00:03:35.418
I can't give you $30,000

00:03:35.418 --> 00:03:37.580
because I think I can negotiate you there

00:03:37.580 --> 00:03:40.260
because the people that
you're gonna be sitting across

00:03:40.260 --> 00:03:42.940
and beside, they all make $50,000.

00:03:42.940 --> 00:03:45.200
So, if you tell me you need $100,000,

00:03:45.200 --> 00:03:47.190
I'm gonna go, it's not gonna work

00:03:47.470 --> 00:03:49.070
'cause I know what
everyone else is making.

00:03:49.070 --> 00:03:52.643
I need you to fit kind of
in a similar bucket, right?

00:03:53.540 --> 00:03:55.350
- Make sure you have at
least three questions

00:03:55.350 --> 00:03:57.540
at the end of your conversation
to ask the recruiter.

00:03:57.540 --> 00:03:58.990
- I think a really good question

00:03:58.990 --> 00:04:00.780
to ask at the end of an interview

00:04:00.780 --> 00:04:02.800
is what can I do in this role

00:04:02.800 --> 00:04:05.400
in the first three
months to be successful?

00:04:05.400 --> 00:04:08.650
- What does the first 30 to
90 days look like in this job?

00:04:08.650 --> 00:04:10.760
- I think that gives you
the perfect framework

00:04:10.760 --> 00:04:12.770
for what you can do in the future.

00:04:12.770 --> 00:04:13.720
If you get the job,

00:04:13.810 --> 00:04:15.480
you'll basically have a cheat sheet

00:04:15.480 --> 00:04:18.080
for what you need to do in
your first couple months.

00:04:19.510 --> 00:04:23.153
- If you don't get the job,
don't stalk me, it's over.

00:04:23.360 --> 00:04:26.110
- The stalker scenario is when a candidate

00:04:26.110 --> 00:04:28.490
does not understand why
they didn't get the job

00:04:28.700 --> 00:04:30.740
and they follow you on Instagram,

00:04:30.740 --> 00:04:31.920
they follow you on Facebook.

00:04:31.920 --> 00:04:35.143
- I definitely had a guy, and
this guy could not let it go.

00:04:35.170 --> 00:04:38.210
He showed up to the office
wanting to talk to me.

00:04:38.210 --> 00:04:41.100
- A connection on LinkedIn,
fine, that's cool, but that's...

00:04:41.100 --> 00:04:42.890
Anything more than that,
you crossed the line.

00:04:42.890 --> 00:04:47.890
- I get not a Facebook message,
not an Instagram message,

00:04:48.150 --> 00:04:51.890
he messages me on LinkedIn
and asks me out on a date

00:04:52.350 --> 00:04:54.500
after we turned him down for an interview.

00:04:54.500 --> 00:04:55.670
He did not get the job,

00:04:55.670 --> 00:04:58.200
and he definitely did not get the date.

00:04:58.200 --> 00:05:00.240
Keep reaching out to people on LinkedIn,

00:05:00.240 --> 00:05:02.010
keep expanding your network.

00:05:02.010 --> 00:05:03.927
There is a job out there for you.

00:05:04.262 --> 00:05:06.845
(upbeat music)

